{
  "id": 488923751,
  "iid": 25106,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "UDP: Don't resend data to the follow tap in proxy protocols",
  "description": "Proxy protocols call decode_udp_ports, similar to decode_tcp_ports.\nNeither of these functions create a new stream ID.\n\nIn the TCP case, decode_tcp_ports does not send data to the follow\ntap, but in the UDP case, decode_udp_ports does. The former handling\nis more correct; the latter ends up sending the proxy payload twice,\nonce including the proxy header from the UDP dissector, and again\nwhen the proxy dissector calls decode_udp_ports. This might make sense\nif a different stream ID was associated with the proxy payload, but\nit is not, so there's double payload for the same stream ID.\n\nHave the UDP dissector do the same thing as the TCP dissector, and send\nto the follow stream before calling decode_udp_ports.\n\nThe capture files in #19237 can be used to demonstrate the behavior.\n(Note that \"try heuristic dissectors first\" must be enabled to detect\nthe PROXY protocol there.)\n\nPing #18231\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
